 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "The rules",
   "span": "full",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "class": "methods",
     "head": [
      "Rule",
      "What it gives",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "All radii of a circle are equal",
       "two radii + a chord = an **isosceles** triangle",
       "diameter $30\\Rightarrow r=15$"
      ],
      [
       "Central angle $=2\\times$ inscribed angle (same arc)",
       "stand at the vertex: the arc you see is its arc",
       "central $100°\\Rightarrow$ inscribed $50°$"
      ],
      [
       "Inscribed angles on the same arc are equal",
       "move the vertex along the circle: the angle stays",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "An inscribed angle on a diameter is $90°$",
       "a right triangle in a circle: its hypotenuse is a diameter",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "Inscribed quadrilateral: opposite angles add up to $180°$",
       "all four vertices must be on the circle",
       "$65°\\Rightarrow115°$"
      ],
      [
       "Trapezoid in a circle: always **isosceles**",
       "same leg $180°$ + opposite $180°$: equal base angles",
       "$70°$: $\\angle D=\\angle C=110°$"
      ],
      [
       "The perpendicular from the center halves a chord",
       "$d^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{chord}}{2}\\right)^2=r^2$",
       "$r=17,\\ d=8\\Rightarrow$ chord $30$"
      ],
      [
       "Equal chords $\\Leftrightarrow$ equal arcs $\\Leftrightarrow$ equal central angles",
       "",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "Radius to the touching point $\\perp$ tangent",
       "see a tangent: draw that radius",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "Two tangents from one point are equal",
       "with the radii: a kite with two right angles",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "Touching circles: join the centers",
       "outside: $R+r$; one inside the other: $R-r$",
       ""
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
