  {
   "title": "Advanced tools",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "Shaded areas: **what minus what?** A segment is a sector minus a triangle. Nested shapes: square-circle-square and circle-square-circle **twice**, triangle-circle-triangle **four times**, circle-triangle-circle (equilateral) **four times**: $R=2r$, the ring is 3 small circles. Radii and tangents make right, **gold** ($30°$-$60°$-$90°$) and **silver** ($45°$-$45°$-$90°$) triangles; two radii with $60°$ make an equilateral triangle. They ask for a total? Find the total directly."
    }
